      "given": "$m = 10\\text{ kg}$, $s = 5\\text{ m}$, $\\theta = 37^\\circ$, $\\mu_k = 0.2$, $g = 10\\text{ m/s}^2$.",
      "formula": "F(\\cos\\theta + \\mu_k \\sin\\theta) = \\mu_k mg, \\quad W = F s \\cos\\theta",
      "stepByStep": "1. Normal force $N = 10(10) - F(0.6) = 100 - 0.6F$.\n2. $F(0.8) = 0.2(100 - 0.6F) = 20 - 0.12F \\implies 0.92F = 20 \\implies F = 20/0.92 = 21.74\\text{ N}$.\n3. Work done $W = F s \\cos 37^\\circ = (21.74)(5)(0.8) = 86.96\\text{ J}$.",
